Patches applied to the pristine attr-2.6.0 tarball by ../unpack.sh.

They apply with `patch -p1` from inside src/, in filename order.  Each one
starts with a few lines of prose saying what it does and why, then the diff.

  0001-xattrat-syscall-header-only-with-syscalls.patch
        libmisc/xattrat.c includes the header defining struct xattr_args
        only when the *xattrat system call numbers exist; without them its
        stand-ins answer ENOSYS and never use the structure.

  0002-proc-self-fd-likeos-descriptor-paths.patch
        A name relative to a directory descriptor (getfattr -R, setfattr -R,
        setfattr --restore) is reached through the path the descriptor was
        opened with, read from the /proc/self/fd/N link, instead of through
        /proc/self/fd/N/<name>, which the path walk does not cross.

